=== BR-AR-0019 REOPENING (third pass): Defect A (walk every eager ref, tag version_status) and Defect B
    (harness-METHOD dispatch, the dominant real shape) ===

--- Mechanism ---
Defect A: govbridge/code/lineage_layer.py now selects its eager ref set via govbridge.code.build.eager_ref_names
(reused, never re-derived -- RefSpec.role/layers, never a ref NAME), walks EVERY ref it returns (on the real
config/canonical-view.yaml: records, product, evidence), and tags every persisted row with its own
(ref_name, commit_id, version_status, canonical_ref, canonical_commit) via _version_status, which mirrors
govbridge.core.view.ResolvedView.classify_occurrence exactly (a measured data-source substitution, not a parallel
algorithm -- see its own docstring and tests/code/test_lineage_layer.py::test_version_status_agrees_with_
classify_occurrence).
Defect B: govbridge/code/rust_cli.py gains find_impl_wrapper_methods (an inherent impl method taking a &[&str]/
&[String] parameter, "direct"/"forward" classified exactly like a free-function wrapper) and
_resolve_harness_receiver (the calling test's own `let`-declared local variable types, via _local_var_types; a
receiver whose type cannot be determined falls back to a method name unique across every harness type this build
found -- an ambiguous name is recorded to lineage_unresolved, form="rust_harness_method", never silently dropped).

